#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074600} :activity/id #uuid "405276f7-9827-5091-903e-512c9c2ab67a" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049418 :topic/id #uuid "f344db4d-49a0-59ae-b874-a20de566b228" :topic/math-academy-id 485} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074600 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186075050 :tutorial/content "In the coordinate plane, the **midpoint** of a line segment with endpoints $(x_1,y_1)$ and $(x_2,y_2)$ lies halfway between the $x$-coordinates $x_1$ and $x_2$, and halfway between the $y$-coordinates $y_1$ and $y_2$.\n\nThe coordinates of the midpoint can be computed using the formula\n\n$$\n(x_m,y_m) = \\left(\\dfrac{x_1 +x_2}2,\\dfrac{y_1+y_2}2\\right)\n$$\n\nFor example, the coordinates of the midpoint of a line segment with endpoints $(2,1)$ and $(6,13)$ can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x_{m}, y_{m}) &= (\\frac{x_{1} + x_{2}}{2}, \\frac{y_{1} + y_{2}}{2}) \\\\\n&= (\\frac{2 + 6}{2}, \\frac{1 + 13}{2}) \\\\\n&= (\\frac{8}{2}, \\frac{14}{2}) \\\\\n&= (4, 7)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "164a0bd6-c234-5906-82c5-f00aefe19504" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8897 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "eecc366e-853e-52a8-bc68-b16fc245ecce" :step/math-academy-id 154975 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074601}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074601 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073713 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073483 :question/id #uuid "68fc6ab1-0c7b-50b2-b541-137be5f5572e" :question/math-academy-id "e-14356"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92c49ea0-7ec5-5ffc-8a36-c4f46f78fda7" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050476} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050517}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074065} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074170} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233438} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233493} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233630}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Midpoint of a Segment"} :step/id #uuid "ee2327aa-02a2-5e9b-b07c-07c22671f4fc" :step/math-academy-id 154976 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074602}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074602 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073714 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073484 :question/id #uuid "ca03fd37-a09e-5546-95a5-12f0cd1657c6" :question/math-academy-id "e-14358"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "58e2e40e-209b-5bc7-98df-11841c2bbcc3" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074019} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074066} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074071} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233202} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233637} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233638} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233639} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234357} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290348} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290349} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290350} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342069} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564473} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564537}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Midpoint of a Segment With Variable Coordinates"} :step/id #uuid "a966a4b4-4e42-5a47-812c-3a495619e03c" :step/math-academy-id 154979 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074603}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074603 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186075051 :tutorial/content "Suppose $M(4,2)$ is the midpoint between $A(1,1)$ and $B(a,b)$. What are the values of $a$ and $b$?\n\n![](images/d9/d946b98f81c7f30ff5a277c337be47dc743de531e3b138795d4a15f34ad82d54.png)\n\nAgain, we use the midpoint formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x_{m}, y_{m}) &= (\\frac{x_{1} + x_{2}}{2}, \\frac{y_{1} + y_{2}}{2})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} &= 1, & y_{1}|= 1, \\\\ x_{2}|= a, & y_{2}|= b, \\\\ x_{m}|= 4, & y_{m}|= 2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the known values in the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(4, 2) &= (\\frac{1 + a}{2}, \\frac{1 + b}{2})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the $x$-coordinates equal to each other and the $y$-coordinates equal to each other, we have the following two equations:\n\n$$\n{4 = \\frac{1 + a}{2}; 2 = \\frac{1 + b}{2}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equations by $2$, we have:\n\n$$\n{8 = 1 + a; 4 = 1 + b\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve both equations independently:\n\n$$\n{a = 8 - 1 = 7; b = 4 - 1 = 3\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=7$ and $b=3$." :tutorial/id #uuid "34ecfb6d-a13d-5bc2-b346-787701d55aad" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8900 :tutorial/title "Finding the Coordinates of Endpoints"} :step/id #uuid "4b327d3b-e449-5f4a-9b7f-318819c5309f" :step/math-academy-id 154983 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074604}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074604 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073715 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073485 :question/id #uuid "04e5232d-7f2a-5dd7-b08e-666c5cf1aba5" :question/math-academy-id "e-14360"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b6b70eb-df57-5d17-a753-645ccdf94945" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048760}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074067} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074068} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233494} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233640} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233641} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269104} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275140} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515519} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515597} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542138}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of an Endpoint Given the Midpoint"} :step/id #uuid "039589a4-f68f-5959-bc9d-32aaa65805e0" :step/math-academy-id 154984}] :activity/title "Midpoints in the Coordinate Plane" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073922}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046647} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515705} :activity/id #uuid "0883d86e-5541-56ae-8de4-4ac2740940dd" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049418 :topic/id #uuid "f344db4d-49a0-59ae-b874-a20de566b228" :topic/math-academy-id 485} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515650 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515597 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b7b9791-af25-5e90-861e-446399a6a146" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515128}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515128} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b2a52c3-ee42-535e-8b88-9e9ef0d1b7d4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515446} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8c1496a-1064-5406-b667-1268a2be4ad7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515264}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515264} :answer-field/id #uuid "daca740b-bc95-5aa8-be58-811d21d0982f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515499}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c5f766d1-90d4-56be-969c-e0d6ece7eafd" :question/math-academy-id "q-216948" :question/problem "![](images/75/75ea79c4a66a187d5973375c40f49d373cee14f9d15848841616e93a420c6cbd.png)\n\nGiven that $(-3,3)$ is the midpoint of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ above, find the values of $a$ and $b.$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}},\n$\\,b=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "The given points are ${{(a,b)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1},\\,{y}_{1})}$, ${{(0,1)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2},\\,{y}_{2})}$ and ${{(-3,3)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{m},\\,{y}_{m})}.$\n\nWe use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{m},{y}_{m}) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\ (-3,3) & =(\\frac{a+0}{2},\\frac{b+1}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding $x$- and $y$-coordinates in the equation above gives us\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3 &=\\frac{a}{2} \\\\ 3 &=\\frac{b+1}{2}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}a &=-6 \\\\ b &=5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $a=-6$ and $b=5.$"} :step/id #uuid "4abe6353-f41c-5f2e-aa9f-118f96d42a30"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515661 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074071 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bf240b6-f61f-518a-b330-8c680ccea02f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514933}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514933} :answer-field/id #uuid "eee5b7ab-c133-57eb-9614-aeff1522c54c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070332} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7cf5be2-d878-5497-9973-b2239ae30dbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{9b}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515261}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515261} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e65decf-258e-5566-95ef-5b3bd98f8cc1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070333}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "da9fefdc-bf24-5050-9662-b6463d7dc33f" :question/math-academy-id "q-216932" :question/problem "The midpoint of the line segment with endpoints $(a,2b)$ and $(5a,7b)$\n is$\\,($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $({x}_{m},{y}_{m})$ be the midpoint between ${{(p,-3q)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and ${{(-p,7q)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})}.$\n\nWe use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{m},{y}_{m}) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{a+5a}{2},\\frac{2b+7b}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{6a}{2},\\frac{9b}{2}) \\\\  & =(3a,\\frac{9b}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "6a7eee90-2761-51ce-a490-bd435592e5d7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515650}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515663 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233639 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8aad39ba-6db2-56df-800c-230c6458882c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232321}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186232321} :answer-field/id #uuid "1082e8b5-8913-5875-8fe3-ad51c1835a69" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232320} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42ca0cda-c134-5297-8632-955cb72a1ca9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232323}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186232323} :answer-field/id #uuid "35d8314b-9f95-5b94-bfab-fca783b713e6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "41810a95-1f10-5b21-be9b-c2e54027cf53" :question/math-academy-id "q-216930" :question/problem "The midpoint of the line segment with endpoints $(-3a,6b)$ and $(3a,8b)$ is$\\,($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $({x}_{m},{y}_{m})$ be the midpoint between ${{(-3a,6b)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and ${{(3a,8b)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})}.$\n\nWe use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{m},{y}_{m}) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{-3a+3a}{2},\\frac{6b+8b}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{0}{2},\\frac{14b}{2}) \\\\  & =(0,7b)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "6f7eaf96-9084-5973-a1bd-0aea49c8d031" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515661}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515705 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515519 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f0cd083-b85f-5b73-be46-8de81ad9529e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514903} {:answer/id #uuid "3f987373-c5cf-510d-a27d-0b648d09125c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515010} {:answer/id #uuid "93e4a872-764c-5c44-8abe-38d12305d515" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515184} {:answer/id #uuid "abb63ab6-3015-5a1d-98ac-a93a26fa894d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515233} {:answer/id #uuid "be75ab74-ecad-5cde-bccf-db980f3b0d57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515276}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514903} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b988816-8ed1-5b88-adb7-733d9244bffa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515431}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "07669a6a-a7d4-5af3-bbb0-d0ed7db93b62" :question/math-academy-id "q-14364" :question/problem "If the midpoint of the line segment with endpoints $(-5,3)$ and $(a,b)$ is $(1,4),$\nthen $a+b=$" :question/worked-solution "The given points are ${{(-5,3)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1},\\,{y}_{1})},$ ${{(a,b)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2},\\,{y}_{2})}$ and ${{(1,4)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{m},\\,{y}_{m})}\\,.$\n\nWe use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{m},{y}_{m}) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\ (1,4) & =(\\frac{-5+a}{2},\\frac{3+b}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding $x$- and $y$-coordinates in the equation above gives us\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}1 &=\\frac{-5+a}{2} \\\\ 4 &=\\frac{3+b}{2}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}a &=7 \\\\ b &=5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $(a,b)=(7,5)$ and $a+b=12.$"} :step/id #uuid "ee2d3f73-67b1-53f4-89a5-3dc76f78bca8" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515663}}] :activity/title "Midpoints in the Coordinate Plane" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514851}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046647} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542249} :activity/id #uuid "eef3f0e0-2c27-56ab-a4f0-738c634476a3" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049418 :topic/id #uuid "f344db4d-49a0-59ae-b874-a20de566b228" :topic/math-academy-id 485} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542249 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542138 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f31f1d9-20ae-587f-a12f-646339ce7532" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541453} {:answer/id #uuid "cafb4598-4e4a-5ef9-8efd-a9be9580151c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541852} {:answer/id #uuid "cd404286-0e08-551f-bf6f-c8bce00a1c38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541856} {:answer/id #uuid "f32c4e39-cea4-50c5-b6e5-5ec6f145d74d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541935} {:answer/id #uuid "fec1d3b2-ad6a-5e33-a76a-9d8f3aab99ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541958}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541453} :answer-field/id #uuid "fae6beff-dfb6-5353-a25e-278027e8d1a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542105}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "43dcffb9-2ca6-59ab-b26c-63732a3440fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-4101" :question/problem "Find $x+y$ if the midpoint of the line segment with endpoints $(x,y)$ and $(5,-4)$ is $(0,6).$" :question/worked-solution "The given points are ${{(x,y)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1},\\,{y}_{1})}$, ${{(5,-4)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2},\\,{y}_{2})}$ and ${{(0,6)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{m},\\,{y}_{m})}.$\n\nFirst, the $x$-coordinate of the midpoint's  must be the average of the $x$-coordinates of the endpoints: \n\n$$\n0=\\frac{x+5}{2}\\,⇒\\,x=-5.\n$$\n\nSimilarly, the $y$-coordinate of the midpoint must be the average of the $y$-coordinates of the endpoints: \n\n$$\n6=\\frac{y+(-4)}{2}\\,⇒\\,y=16.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $(x,y)=(-5,16)$ and $x+y=11.$"} :step/id #uuid "3b557119-31df-578b-8d5c-b8315690625d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542260}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542260 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290348 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0970c009-f049-5fa9-a166-8b84d6ac5fad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value ",2q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288105} {:answer/id #uuid "3863c9ed-b576-5842-ac45-186f38ccce1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541543}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541543} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e665707-0353-515a-aae0-dded2b92c64d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289931} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88ef702a-2405-512b-9fb0-70a241bc1764" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288954}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288954} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff5c4d7e-c117-5b76-9e60-4bd62906faaa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290254}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "31c959b9-6c65-52b7-b42f-0da8b7c0d3f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-216927" :question/problem "The midpoint of the line segment with endpoints $(p,-3q)$ and $(-p,7q)$\n is$\\,($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $({x}_{m},{y}_{m})$ be the midpoint between ${{(p,-3q)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and ${{(-p,7q)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})}.$\n\nWe use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{m},{y}_{m}) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{p+(-p)}{2},\\frac{-3q+7q}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{0}{2},\\frac{4q}{2}) \\\\  & =(0,2q)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "6b660e3d-ccaa-51c3-8391-7e354397a05a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542279}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542279 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233638 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19156b0d-85dd-55bf-92c5-90b05ca8405a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232317}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186232317} :answer-field/id #uuid "664dfe98-66e6-5bae-a9a7-b47a5a5e45f9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232316} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8d59528-68c8-562f-b103-349c4f60afa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232319}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186232319} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2a16269-c3d6-50fd-9b87-ae55cd7d3020" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232318}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9f0c1db7-3670-5389-b242-c12c078528a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-216929" :question/problem "The midpoint of the line segment with endpoints $(4a,-2b)$ and $(-2a,2b)$ is$\\,($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $({x}_{m},{y}_{m})$ be the midpoint between ${{(4a,-2b)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and ${{(-2a,2b)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})}.$\n\nWe use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{m},{y}_{m}) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{4a+(-2a)}{2},\\frac{-2b+2b}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{2a}{2},\\frac{0}{2}) \\\\  & =(a,0)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "dd208b46-0969-55b1-9e6c-c7f5674d3754"}] :activity/title "Midpoints in the Coordinate Plane" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541424}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046647} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564550} :activity/id #uuid "16e1fd21-d537-5ae9-9de0-7f106ce3512a" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049418 :topic/id #uuid "f344db4d-49a0-59ae-b874-a20de566b228" :topic/math-academy-id 485} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564548 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564473 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13df7405-37a9-5376-a794-b50ade14b257" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(2p,-5q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563997} {:answer/id #uuid "2248598d-8d45-5b33-a1bb-161e7e022f16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(2p,-4q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564017} {:answer/id #uuid "41743567-93b3-52b5-956f-5e3cf584ae66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(6p,-5q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564079} {:answer/id #uuid "b2dfc1f4-7244-51d1-b08e-beaf085cffe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(3p,-5q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564249} {:answer/id #uuid "cd30a56d-8702-5fad-b81c-b55db3829574" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(4p,-2q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564290}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564249} :answer-field/id #uuid "47c69590-b35f-5b4e-b1cf-478ea7e99763" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564392}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1a0af22d-5fcd-5a62-b138-4a5969bb9fc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-73730" :question/problem "Find the midpoint of the line segment with endpoints $(8p,-q)$ and $(-2p,-9q).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $({x}_{m},{y}_{m})$ be the midpoint between ${{(8p,-q)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and ${{(-2p,-9q)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})}.$\n\nWe use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{m},{y}_{m}) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{8p+(-2p)}{2},\\frac{-q+(-9q)}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{8p-2p}{2},\\frac{-q-9q}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{6p}{2},\\frac{-10q}{2}) \\\\  & =(3p,-5q).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "2022c43f-bf94-523c-aa78-e657d9fc756e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564584}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564550 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564537 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00b86450-d396-50c2-b792-96eb2e069dee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-w,-z)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563969} {:answer/id #uuid "1707b2e5-7f13-581b-928d-cb954858885d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(2w,2z)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563999} {:answer/id #uuid "2295ae60-1e26-5128-8f27-466b06ffd6c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(2w,3z)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564018} {:answer/id #uuid "2c117928-80a8-595c-9b86-d8c72d7f0afb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-2w,-2z)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564039} {:answer/id #uuid "c0661565-ff3d-5e5e-b035-22e247858f0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-w,2z)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564264}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563999} :answer-field/id #uuid "87c637ca-477b-51e8-ad73-42e7989eff3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564417}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f548e29c-4fb0-5de0-8aa0-2659faa5a2eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-73720" :question/problem "Find the midpoint of the line segment with endpoints $(-w,7z)$ and $(5w,-3z).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $({x}_{m},{y}_{m})$ be the midpoint between ${{(-w,7z)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and ${{(5w,-3z)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})}.$\n\nWe use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{m},{y}_{m}) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{-w+5w}{2},\\frac{7z+(-3z)}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{-w+5w}{2},\\frac{7z-3z}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{4w}{2},\\frac{4z}{2}) \\\\  & =(2w,2z).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "20c277f2-75f7-54cc-82c6-c8c4fe25dff4" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564548}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564584 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233640 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49fac7bf-46ec-5ac8-9e60-c629e9e8013c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232325}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186232325} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4bdca92-d3ce-5317-93a5-453116878ba3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232324} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "957e3eaa-ef13-506d-8623-b2a325befa53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232327}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186232327} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc196177-57eb-5ab4-b3b9-ccd45d691c3c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232326}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "916ab087-cc91-5679-86a8-6caf3720561e" :question/math-academy-id "q-216947" :question/problem "![](images/22/226b832db682da8379d9567123974abb3d44c02f4db3c3ef78d48c1a8f2a491e.png)\n\nGiven that $(1,1)$ is the midpoint of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ above, find the values of $a$ and $b.$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}},\n$\\,b=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "The given points are ${{(a,b)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1},\\,{y}_{1})}$, ${{(-2,0)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2},\\,{y}_{2})}$ and ${{(1,1)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{m},\\,{y}_{m})}.$\n\nWe use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{m},{y}_{m}) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\ (1,1) & =(\\frac{a-2}{2},\\frac{b+0}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding $x$- and $y$-coordinates in the equation above gives us\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}1 &=\\frac{a-2}{2} \\\\ 1 &=\\frac{b}{2}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\Rightarrow \\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}a &=4 \\\\ b &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $a=4$ and $b=2.$"} :step/id #uuid "be38ad57-685f-57cb-91ce-666c45d052ff"}] :activity/title "Midpoints in the Coordinate Plane" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563958}]}
